{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/101443-homebrew-token-the-rumor-mill","id":101443,"title":"Homebrew token: The Rumor Mill","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-29T13:07:29-07:00","id":101443,"title":"Homebrew token: The Rumor Mill","content":"I came up with this on another forum, but I can't find the old writeup so I've rewritten it. Looking for some constructive criticism!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Rumor Mill</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This Token\u2019s Mask appears to be an old, grimy pepper mill, of the sort used in restaurants. If opened, it is empty, and the inside appears crusted with a disgusting film of rotted food and other, less savory substances. A character may whisper a name (such as \u201cJoe Connelly\u201d or \u201cTommy O\u2019Tinder\u201d) or a subject (such as \u201cThe Summer Court\u2019s new compound out west.\u201d) into the opened mill, then close it, trapping the words inside. If the mill is then held up to the ear and ground, it whispers three pieces of information about the subject, chosen by the Storyteller. This is always information known to at least three people other than the subject of the secrets. The True Fae are never valid subjects for the use of this Token. Indeed, attempting to do so grants the Gentry in question the benefit of the token in regards to the character - and the Gentry have had long years learning to tell truth from fiction.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appropriate information to gain include skills or capabilities (\u201cMartin the Short pretends to be helpless in a fight, but he\u2019s actually pretty deadly with a knife\u201d), social ties (\u201cOphidia was just elected head of the board of directors on St. Joseph\u2019s hospital\u201d), recent activities (\u201cRobin Dobbin has been seen entering and exiting the Hedge through the gate in the 7-11 bathroom quite often lately\u201d) and other information (\u201cThe Cave has a library hidden in the very back, behind a false rock wall. There\u2019s a lock and some booby traps to keep it safe.\u201d) (\u201cWalter has suffered severe depression since the death of his favorite hound last month\u201d). The information is given in rumor form, without specific game-term knowledge; for example, a player might determine from the first rumor above that Martin the Short has decent Weaponry skill, but wouldn\u2019t know his precise rating. This Token may only be used once per month on any given subject.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mien:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> When active, the mill becomes shiny and new, decorated in unsettling spiral patterns. The burr grinders at the mill\u2019s base disappear, replaced by sharp, white teeth which chatter and bite as they whisper their secrets.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Drawback:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Only two of the pieces of information imparted by the Mill are true secrets. One piece of information is always false, usually something that will lead to strife and trouble for the Token\u2019s user if followed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Catch:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The Mill speaks its secrets quietly, forcing the user to hold it close to his ear in order to hear. This gives the teeth a chance to bite at the user\u2019s ear, dealing 1 point of lethal damage and inflicting a -1 penalty to rolls involving hearing until the damage is healed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Edits: Removed the second drawback, imposed a limit of one use per month per subject, and noted that the True Fae are invalid subjects for this token (and attempting it is a Very Bad Idea)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 03-29-2014, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:13:42-07:00","id":101449,"title":"","content":"Awesome!<br /> <br /> You sort of have two Drawbacks. So I'd keep only the one about 1/3 being trouble. It seems too powerful to let you make someone's deepest secrets public knowledge like this.<br /> <br /> I would also add a contested roll. A True Fae's secrets should be hard to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T15:24:51-07:00","id":101530,"title":"","content":"Hrm... You might be right about the second Drawback. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure what to use for the roll(s) to use this, as the mill itself is doing the work magically. Maybe I'd allow a defense roll, which causes the Token to fail if successful, or maybe I should just stipulate that the True Fae aren't valid subjects (and trying gives them rumors of the user).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T16:33:08-07:00","id":101588,"title":"","content":"I love this Token in its revised form. Good job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}